From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:07:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Athena API: say who owns a player after a move across
 threads, and lock events until worlds have threads

teleportAsync completes once a player handed to another world's thread is in
that world, on that thread; the javadoc says what may follow a cross-thread
teleport, that a kick from any thread works even when the player's world is
stuck, that reading a world belongs on its thread too, and that a stop which
times out hands the world back later. SimplePluginManager calls synchronous
events under its lock again until the first world thread starts
(athenaLockFree), as Bukkit does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
index 5d88087e9642deb286dc64033db6f630c5809fc9..75efaad9c6a0cd3d2d0570d422704c9e082787b6 100644
--- a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
+++ b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
@@ -227,8 +227,15 @@ public final class Athena {
      * from any thread. It does not make the work after the teleport any lighter: for many players at
      * once, see {@link #teleportGradually(List, List, int)}.
      *
+     * <p>A player moved into a world that another thread ticks is handed over: {@code Player.teleport}
+     * returns as soon as the player has left, and from then on only the new world's thread may touch
+     * the player. This future completes once the player is in the new world, on that world's thread,
+     * so what follows the move belongs in {@code thenAccept}.
+     *
      * @return completes on the thread that ticks the entity's world: true if the entity was
-     *         teleported, false if it was gone by then or a plugin cancelled the teleport
+     *         teleported, false if it was gone by then or a plugin cancelled the teleport; for a player
+     *         handed to another thread, true once it is in the new world (false if that world went away
+     *         meanwhile and the player was sent to the main world instead)
      */
     public static CompletableFuture<Boolean> teleportAsync(Entity entity, Location location) {
         return getServer().teleportAsync(entity, location);
@@ -410,20 +417,29 @@ public final class Athena {
     /**
      * Moves {@code world}'s ticking off the server thread onto a thread of its own. A stall in that
      * world (a slow listener, a long chunk load) then holds up that world alone, and the server
-     * thread and the other worlds keep ticking. From then on only that thread may touch the world:
-     * use {@link #runOnWorld} to work on it from elsewhere. Aikar's timings are turned off.
+     * thread and the other worlds keep ticking. From then on only that thread may touch the world -
+     * reading it too: {@code World.getPlayers()} and {@code getEntities()} walk lists that thread
+     * changes. Use {@link #runOnWorld} to work on it from elsewhere. Aikar's timings are turned off.
      *
      * <p>Players in the world go with it: their packets, connection ticks, commands, chat
      * callbacks and quits run on the world's thread. A player moves between worlds ticked by
      * different threads in two steps: it leaves on its old world's thread and arrives on the new
      * one's, so {@code teleport} returns before the player is there, and a player on the way cannot
-     * be teleported again. A login aimed at such a world lands in the main world and is then moved.
+     * be teleported again. After such a {@code teleport} the calling thread no longer owns the player:
+     * {@code getLocation} already answers the destination, but changes to the player (effects, game
+     * mode, inventory) belong after {@link #teleportAsync}'s future, which completes on the new
+     * world's thread once the player is there. A player headed for a world that is unloaded or halted
+     * meanwhile lands at the main world's spawn. A login aimed at such a world lands in the main world
+     * and is then moved.
      * Other entities move the same way: written out and removed on the old world's thread, made again
      * on the new one's (riders and leashes stay behind). The main world cannot have its own thread.
      *
      * <p>Vanilla commands then run on the server thread with every world thread waiting between two
      * ticks, since they may touch any world; one typed in a world on its own thread runs a moment
-     * later. A scoreboard may be changed from any thread, and so may who hides whom.
+     * later. A scoreboard may be changed from any thread, and so may who hides whom. A kick from
+     * another thread is passed on to the player's world's thread; if that thread is stuck (see
+     * {@link athena.api.event.WorldThreadStallEvent}), the server thread disconnects the player
+     * itself, so a stuck world never keeps its players from leaving or logging in again.
      *
      * @throws IllegalStateException if {@code world} is the main world, or this is called from inside
      *         the world's own tick
@@ -436,7 +452,8 @@ public final class Athena {
      * Hands {@code world}'s ticking back to the server thread: waits up to 10 seconds for its thread
      * to finish the tick it is in. Unloading a world does this itself.
      *
-     * @return false if the thread did not stop in time; it then still owns the world
+     * @return false if the thread did not stop in time; it then still owns the world until its tick
+     *         ends, and hands the world back to the server thread by itself then
      */
     public static boolean stopWorldThread(World world) {
         return getServer().stopWorldThread(world);
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/plugin/SimplePluginManager.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/plugin/SimplePluginManager.java
index 1ac53c91397bfba3c5d57eb1342374751f8fad54..457d472d093ed1df14962020b5234c36735e420d 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/plugin/SimplePluginManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/plugin/SimplePluginManager.java
@@ -535,6 +535,12 @@ public final class SimplePluginManager implements PluginManager {
      *
      * @param event Event details
      */
+    /**
+     * Athena - set by the server when the first world starts ticking on its own thread: synchronous
+     * events are no longer called under one lock from then on. Until then, as in Bukkit.
+     */
+    public static volatile boolean athenaLockFree;
+
     public void callEvent(Event event) {
         if (event.isAsynchronous()) {
             if (Thread.holdsLock(this)) {
@@ -544,12 +550,16 @@ public final class SimplePluginManager implements PluginManager {
                 throw new IllegalStateException(event.getEventName() + " cannot be triggered asynchronously from primary server thread.");
             }
             fireEvent(event);
-        } else {
-            // Athena - no lock: worlds that tick on their own threads call their events at the same
+        } else if (athenaLockFree) {
+            // Athena - no lock once worlds tick on their own threads: they call their events at the same
             // time, and one world stuck in a listener must not hold up the others' events. The
             // handler lists are already safe to read from any thread (HandlerList bakes them under
             // its own lock); listeners that share state between worlds must guard it themselves.
             fireEvent(event);
+        } else {
+            synchronized (this) {
+                fireEvent(event);
+            }
         }
     }
 
